      'Setup example: 10 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Win points by ending hands with lower deadwood than opponent and reach game target first.',
      'Turn-flow example: On each turn draw one card from stock or top discard, then discard one card face up. If you took the top discard this turn, you cannot discard that same card immediately. Melds are sets (3-4 equal ranks) and runs (3+ same-suit consecutive cards); a card cannot count in two melds at once. Ace is always low, so A-2-3 is valid but A-K-Q is not. A player may knock after drawing if deadwood is 10 or less by discarding face down, then both hands are exposed. If knocker did not go gin, opponent may lay off unmatched cards on knocker melds. If stock reaches two cards and no one has knocked, hand is cancelled and redealt.',
      'Scoring example: Hand scoring uses deadwood difference plus bonus events, and game scoring continues across hands. Reach 100 or more cumulative points first, then apply game and line bonuses..',
